Here we show the queries (via cone search in Gaia) used to obtain the stars we want to study. 
We made sure to use a bigger angular size than the one of the clusters to also retrieve field stars and 
be able to show a valuable cleaning and selecting process of stars in the clusters.

Query NGC104:
<INFO name="QUERY" value="SELECT 
    dr3.source_id,
    dr3.ra, dr3.dec,
    dr3.l, dr3.b,
    dr3.parallax, dr3.parallax_error,
    dr3.parllax_over_error,
    dr3.pm,
    dr3.pmra, dr3.pmra_error,
    dr3.pmdec, dr3.pmdec_error,
    dr3.phot_g_mean_mag,
    dr3.phot_bp_mean_mag,
    dr3.phot_rp_mean_mag,
    dr3.bp_rp,
    dr3.astrometric_excess_noise,
    dr3.phot_bp_rp_excess_factor,
    dr3.ruwe,
    dr3.teff_gspphot,
    dr3.logg_gspphot,
    dr3.mh_gspphot,
    dr3.phot_variable_flag,
    dr3.visibility_periods_used
FROM gaiadr3.gaia_source AS dr3
WHERE 1 = CONTAINS(
    POINT(&#039;ICRS&#039;, dr3.ra, dr3.dec),
    CIRCLE(&#039;ICRS&#039;, 6.023625, -72.081283, 1.1));


